hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28014","Narrated Abdullah ibn Numayr, he said: narrated Musa Al-Juhani, he said: Fatimah bint Ali narrated to me, she said: Asma bint Umays narrated to me, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Ali, you are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."
"28015","Narrated Abu Kamil and Yazid ibn Harun and Affan, they said: narrated Muhammad ibn Talhah, Yazid said in his hadith: narrated Al-Hakam, and Affan said in his hadith: I heard Al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Asma bint Umays, she said: When Jafar was killed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and said: O mother, wear mourning garments for three days, then do what you wish."
"28016","Abdullah said: and narrated Muhammad ibn Bakkar, he said: narrated Muhammad ibn Talhah likewise."
"28017","Narrated Abdur-Razzaq, he said: narrated Mamar, from Az-Zuhri, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Al-Harith ibn Hisham informed me, from Asma bint Umays, she said: The first time the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complained was in the house of Maymunah, then his illness became severe until he fainted, so his wives consulted about giving him medicine in the side of the mouth, so they gave him ladud. When he recovered he said: What is this? So we said: This is the deed of women who came from here, and he pointed toward the land of Abyssinia, and Asma bint Umays was among them. They said: We suspected pleurisy in you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: That is an ailment Allah Almighty would never afflict me with. No one shall remain in this house except he is given ladud, except the uncle of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), meaning Al-Abbas. He said: Maymunah was given ladud that day though she was fasting, due to the resolve of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"28018","Narrated Sufyan, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Urwah ibn Amir, from Ubayd ibn Rifaah Az-Zuraqi, he said: Asma said: O Messenger of Allah, the sons of Jafar are struck by the evil eye, shall I seek ruqyah for them? He said: Yes, for if anything were to precede the decree, the eye would precede it."
"28019","Narrated Uthman ibn Umar, he said: narrated Yunus meaning Ibn Yazid Al-Ayli, he said: narrated Abu Shaddad, from Mujahid, from Asma bint Umays, she said: I was the companion of Aishah who prepared her and brought her in to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with me were women. She said: By Allah, we found no hospitality with him except a cup of milk. She said: So he drank from it then handed it to Aishah, and the girl was shy, so we said: Do not refuse the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), take from it. So she took it shyly and drank from it, then he said: Hand to your companions. So we said: We do not desire it. So he said: Do not combine hunger and lying. She said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, if one of us says of something she desires, I do not desire it, is that counted as lying? He said: Lying is written as lying, until the small lie is written as a small lie."
